  "marks": {
    "tatter": {
      "x": 2700,
      "y": 3840,
      "facing": 1,
      "want": [2620, 1460],
      "until": "wood-firefly-glimpse"
    },
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 3484,
        "text": "THE OAK (wood-hollow): the hollow at its foot, the trunk, the crown: one room, no seam (plan r3 item 3)"
      },
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 3544,
        "text": "W: in from wood-glidewalk at floor level"
      },
      {
        "x": 1150,
        "y": 3604,
        "text": "P3 moon patch. THE GLIMPSE (hold 300): the camera rises the trunk to the crown; the firefly hangs W-ff; Tatter leads her out. The east arch is shut until it has played"
      },
      {
        "x": 1700,
        "y": 3764,
        "text": "the MOTH-STONE: the area on the map; its carving: moths climbing the oak"
      },
      {
        "x": 2200,
        "y": 3764,
        "text": "the first firefly sign at the trunk's foot: a ring of picked glow-cap stumps"
      },
      {
        "x": 2580,
        "y": 3944,
        "text": "the root mesh (one-way; no drop-through until wood-climbout): up from the climb-out, then the shortcut down to P4"
      },
      {
        "x": 2580,
        "y": 3200,
        "text": "catch rungs across the column every ~550 (one-ways: she kicks up through them, a fall lands on one)"
      },
      {
        "x": 3300,
        "y": 3764,
        "text": "E arch: the one way on before the claws, east to the hawkers' clearing"
      },
      {
        "x": 2200,
        "y": 2300,
        "text": "REST LEDGE: W-rest's cut spots; dang-knot drops on them from under the bridge"
      },
      {
        "x": 2700,
        "y": 2200,
        "text": "P-ledge (moon patch) on the buttress, out of W-rest's light; the column's east face is slick under it"
      },
      {
        "x": 2960,
        "y": 1780,
        "text": "the near face holds from P-ledge up to the floor under W-ff; slick above it, then holds again from the shelf"
      },
      {
        "x": 2300,
        "y": 1830,
        "text": "the floor under W-ff (one-way): stand under it, out of its pull; hop up into it: the catch is a choice"
      },
      {
        "x": 2380,
        "y": 1560,
        "text": "W-ff (lit after the glimpse): caught, beat free up-left: thrown onto the knot bridge"
      },
      {
        "x": 2140,
        "y": 1270,
        "text": "the knot bridge: from its tip, walk off and down-cut W-ff (pogo snuff); on to the foothold on the face"
      },
      {
        "x": 1480,
        "y": 1080,
        "text": "FIND: bark knot, W-knot behind it"
      },
      {
        "x": 3000,
        "y": 250,
        "text": "the crown wick on the rim's walk (a standing cut, like R3's knob); hawk-crown swoops through its orbit over the rim; snuffed, it leaves before the finale"
      },
      {
        "x": 3090,
        "y": 360,
        "text": "the root's knot (one cut): the root falls down the trunk; Tatter climbs"
      },
      {
        "x": 3380,
        "y": 330,
        "text": "P5, THE CROWN (finale hold 540, the trigger the rim's full height: no way to the exit but through it): the look-out, the cloud lifts off"
      },
      {
        "x": 3010,
        "y": 3520,
        "text": "THE TRUNK'S FOOT: Tatter goes in at the crack (bark, 3 cuts); inside, W-foot with three stragglers (the oak's first snuff, the moths spiral up the trunk), the night eyes hollow, Tatter in the moonlight; the passage under the flare's roof is the way east"
      },
      {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 3330,
        "text": "root curtains hang from the hollow roof (overhangs only: no ledge a bot or a player can see and not reach)"
      }
    ],
